{
  "_about": "Component spec for pos-checkbox (docs/inspect refactor, component migration batch, 2026-08-26). Single source of truth for the Variants/Usage/Tokens tabs on /style-guide \"Checkbox\" section. Reuses the already-curated usage prose from COMP_CONFIGS['checkbox'].usage and token data from COMP_CONFIGS['checkbox'].tokens (verified-accurate, currently-live data) restructured into the new schema. Single representative variant — this component's preview shows one instance (no Variant/Base toggle needed per the 2026-08-25/26 \"multiple sub-variants side by side\" rule). Regenerate the spec partial with the script in RULES.md 6.4 if the source data changes; do not hand-edit token values here. Updated 2026-08-27: added usageExample/props/composedOf (Target architecture point 1 fields that were left empty when this spec was first generated). 2026-10-02: hover while checked darkens to --pos-color-interactive-hover (it had no hover feedback). Disabled checked fill/frame borrows the primary button disabled tokens (--pos-color-button-primary-disabled-background / -frame) — documented exception to RULES.md 2.2, see COMPONENT-RULES.md.",
  "component": "checkbox",
  "name": "Checkbox",
  "description": "Selecting zero or more independent options from a list.",
  "whenToUse": [
    "Selecting zero or more independent options from a list.",
    "Toggling a single boolean setting (e.g. \"Remember me\", \"Agree to terms\")."
  ],
  "whenNotToUse": [
    "Exactly one option must be selected — use radio buttons instead.",
    "The toggle is part of a larger interactive card — use <code>pos-switch-card</code> instead."
  ],
  "do": [
    "Always associate a visible <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> with each checkbox via <code>for</code>/<code>id</code>.",
    "Mark required checkboxes with the <code>required</code> attribute.",
    "Use a <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code> with a <code>&lt;legend&gt;</code> when grouping related checkboxes."
  ],
  "dont": [
    "Use for mutually exclusive choices — that is what radio buttons are for.",
    "Rely on visual proximity alone to associate the label — always use <code>for</code>/<code>id</code>."
  ],
  "accessibility": [
    "Each checkbox must have an associated <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> so screen readers announce its purpose.",
    "Use <code>aria-required=\"true\"</code> or the <code>required</code> attribute on required checkboxes.",
    "Group related checkboxes in a <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code> with a <code>&lt;legend&gt;</code>."
  ],
  "composedOf": [],
  "props": [
    {
      "name": "disabled",
      "type": "boolean attribute",
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Native disabled attribute — switches to the disabled color set."
    },
    {
      "name": "checked",
      "type": "boolean attribute",
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Native checked attribute — selected state, shows the checkmark icon."
    }
  ],
